# A `given … with` method closing over a top-level `val`

Executable record of BUGS.md `given-with-method-cannot-close-over-a-top-level-val`, which
carried no gate. `precision` is an ordinary top-level `val`; the `given`'s method body reads
it. Declared `known-red` on the failing lanes so that fixing the defect turns the suite red
and brings whoever fixed it back here to delete the declaration.

```scalascript
trait Sized[A]:
  def size: Int

val precision = 4

given intSized: Sized[Int] with
  def size: Int = 1 << precision

def main(): Unit =
  println(intSized.size)

main()
```
